    <section id="manifesto">
      <div class="narrow lede">
        <p class="kicker">01 — Opening</p>
        <p>Zabiha — also spelled dhabiha — is the Islamic method of slaughter. A permitted animal is cut while it is still alive. The slaughterer invokes the name of Allah. The blood is drained. Marketers then call the result humane, halal, and required.</p>
<p>It is a sacrament with a knife. The United States already wrote a humane-slaughter rule. Zabiha lives in the exemption from that rule, not in the rule. This page refuses the exemption as a model for everyone else.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="kicker">The pitch, in their own words</p>
        <blockquote>Zabiha refers to the specific method of slaughtering animals according to Islamic law, ensuring the meat is halal for Muslims. Without zabiha, meat is generally considered non-halal and not permissible for consumption.</blockquote>
        <p class="fine">That paragraph is the whole ask: describe a religious killing rule, declare every other carcass out of bounds, and call the declaration a fact. It is a fact about a doctrine. It is not a fact about American meat.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section>
