        <div class="narrow" style="margin:0">
          <p class="kicker">02</p>
          <h2>Four claims. Four refusals.</h2>
          <p class="deck">The brochure lists four “core principles.” Each one is either theology or a contradiction. None of them is a reason for a republic to retune its meat supply.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="claim-grid"><article class="claim">
        <p class="num">01</p>
        <h3>Permissible species</h3>
        <p class="eyebrow">Their claim</p>
        <p>The animal must be a non-carnivorous species Islamic law has already blessed.</p>
        <p class="eyebrow hot">The refusal</p>
        <p>That is catechism. A fiqh list of lawful animals is not an inspection standard. USDA does not exist to enforce a religious taxonomy, and American grocery law does not become illegitimate when it ignores one.</p>
      </article>
<article class="claim">
        <p class="num">02</p>
        <h3>Humane handling</h3>
        <p class="eyebrow">Their claim</p>
        <p>The animal should be treated humanely, with no abuse allowed.</p>
        <p class="eyebrow hot">The refusal</p>
        <p>The pamphlet says no abuse, then bans the ordinary Western protection: stunning the animal before the cut. You do not get to refuse the anesthetic and advertise the surgery as kind. “Humane” is the sales word. The method is a cut on a conscious animal.</p>
      </article>
<article class="claim">
        <p class="num">03</p>
        <h3>Invocation of God’s name</h3>
        <p class="eyebrow">Their claim</p>
        <p>The slaughterman must invoke the name of God during the slaughter.</p>
        <p class="eyebrow hot">The refusal</p>
        <p>Tasmiyah is worship. It does not change pain, pathogens, temperature, or residue. A spoken divine name is not a critical control point. A country with no establishment of religion does not put prayer on the kill line and call it food safety.</p>
      </article>
<article class="claim">
        <p class="num">04</p>
        <h3>Proper harvesting</h3>
        <p class="eyebrow">Their claim</p>
        <p>The method must minimize pain and adhere to Islamic guidelines.</p>
        <p class="eyebrow hot">The refusal</p>
        <p>If pain is the measure, use stunning. That is what commercial veterinary practice in the West actually uses to make an animal insensible before steel. A slogan about minimal pain that prohibits the tool is false on its face. Islamic guidelines are the constraint. Pain is the casualty.</p>
      </article></div>
